.TH SHOAL-MCP 1 "July 2026" "Shoal 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
shoal-mcp \- expose Shoal through the Model Context Protocol
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B shoal-mcp
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Runs a Model Context Protocol server on standard input and output, connected to a Shoal kernel.
The default tokenless public identity is a restricted agent.
A named or public socket cannot assert local-human authority; use a policy-scoped bearer token for machine access or the private interactive Shoal REPL for human authority.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-socket " PATH"
Connect to an explicit kernel Unix socket instead of discovering one from the session.
.TP
.BI \-\-session " NAME"
Select the session used for socket discovery and attachment.
.TP
.BI \-\-token " TOKEN"
Authenticate as the capability-token principal.
.TP
.BR \-h , " \-\-help"
Print help and exit.
.TP
.BR \-V , " \-\-version"
Print the version and exit.
.SH OUTPUT
Reads and writes Model Context Protocol messages on standard input and output.
Diagnostics are written to standard error.
.SH ERRORS
Invalid arguments, kernel connection or authentication failures,
and protocol-serving failures terminate the process with a nonzero status.
The retired
.B \-\-local-human
option exits with status 2 and migration guidance; it cannot upgrade a public connection.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B SHOAL_SOCKET
Default explicit socket path.
.TP
.B SHOAL_SESSION
Default session name.
.TP
.B SHOAL_TOKEN
Default bearer token.
.SH EXAMPLES
.EX
SHOAL_TOKEN=secret shoal-mcp --session automation
shoal-mcp --socket /run/user/1000/shoal/default.sock
.EE
.SH EXIT STATUS
Returns 0 after an orderly protocol shutdown, 1 for runtime failures, and 2 for invalid arguments.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR shoal (1),
.BR shoal-token (1),
.BR shoal-kernel (1)
